22SEP2024 @hanoihantrakul
At the time of writing, this is the best performing Vocal Music Tokenizer. 
It is improves the WER compared to the previous SOTA ConformerUMM_2255_2375
See this doc: https://bytedance.us.larkoffice.com/docx/D3ZDdxoxUocraTxAozSuFCl2sdc

21AUG2024 @hanoihantrakul
The TTS ROPE recipe is based on YAML's
`recipes/umm/conf/2024_Q2_conf_archives/conformer_tts_rope/umm_stage1_conformer_tts_rope_mixedZHEN2255.yaml`
`recipes/umm/conf/2024_Q2_conf_archives/conformer_tts_rope/umm_stage2_conformer_tts_rope_mixedZHEN2255.yaml`
`recipes/umm/conf/2024_Q2_conf_archives/conformer_tts_rope/umm_stage3_conformer_tts_rope_mixedZHEN2255_Speech2375.yaml`

I use the same configuration but now train on data [2255, 2375, 794]
instead of just [2255,2375]

The main difference with the BigMusic Recipe is in two areas:
1.) The use of TTS ROPE implementation over BigMusic ROPE implementation
2.) The addition of a pitch-loss head. The total number of losses is now
[mel_loss, chroma_loss, ctc_loss, pitch_loss]

In addition, when training on [Vocal Music, Speech, Instrumental Music] we have
to consider the behavior of the following features:
- Chroma: how does this feature react to the 3 different data types?
See this doc https://bytedance.sg.larkoffice.com/docx/DyjYduDyzoBzAKxtUKOlSuNHgMg
- Pitch Hz: how does this signal react to the 3 different data types?
Seed this doc https://bytedance.sg.larkoffice.com/docx/DyjYduDyzoBzAKxtUKOlSuNHgMg
The conclusion is we can apply these chroma and pitch detector to all 3 different data 
types based on visual inspection of the signals. 
